{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"examples/path-05-continuation.path.json","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T16:22:35.763662Z","id":"64f730cf5b3f2df5813382c12fe88af7b11f2934020e9ddc6f3743aa50e38cb1","body":{"detail":"examples/path-05-continuation.path.json:117-120 (and line 7 of examples/path-05-continuation.path.jsonl): step-007 \"Auto-format\" removes `fn default() -> Self {` / `Self::from_env()` / `}` and adds back the identical three lines, so the step changes nothing; `path p render md --input examples/path-05-continuation.path.json` reports it as `src/lib.rs (+3 -3)`. Its header `@@ -28,6 +28,6 @@` covers 5 lines per side, and step-004's header `@@ -27,0 +28,6 @@` (examples/path-05-continuation.path.json:28) covers 5 added lines. The example is linked from the site (site/eleventy.config.js:134-137) as the demonstration of continuation and delegation; a reader checking the diffs against their own producer will find they do not parse as unified diffs.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"35d7daa3041aa7a50f873ba891dff4ec86a011c6a4c3c1dc4a8990f5ea66ebf4"},"suggested_fix":"Make step-007 a real formatting change (e.g. reindent or reorder) and correct both hunk headers to the actual line counts, in both the .json and .jsonl files.","summary":"The example's rustfmt step is a no-op hunk and its hunk headers overstate the line counts","tags":["review","review:pr-354-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"examples/path-05-continuation.path.json","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T16:27:24.925346Z","id":"c5867586dd36ef3401c204b559221caed1cfd07aed7b6e3702baf041e8ebaea9","body":{"detail":"examples/path-05-continuation.path.json:119: `@@ -28,6 +28,6 @@\\n impl Default for Config {\\n-    fn default() -> Self {\\n-        Self::from_env()\\n-    }\\n+    fn default() -> Self {\\n+        Self::from_env()\\n+    }\\n }\\n` — the three removed lines are byte-identical to the three added lines, and each side of the hunk is 5 lines (1 context + 3 + 1 context), not 6. examples/path-05-continuation.path.jsonl:7 carries the same `raw`. examples/path-05-continuation.path.json:30: `@@ -27,0 +28,6 @@` followed by 5 `+` lines, not 6. `./target/debug/path p render md --input examples/path-05-continuation.path.json` reports step-007 as `src/lib.rs (+3 -3)`. site/eleventy.config.js:134-136 lists the file as \"Path: continuation & delegation\" on the examples page. `suggestion` is right: an example-quality problem, not a parser failure.","kind":"comment","references":"64f730cf5b3f2df5813382c12fe88af7b11f2934020e9ddc6f3743aa50e38cb1","summary":"confirmed: step-007's hunk is a no-op and both cited hunk headers overstate their line counts","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"examples/path-05-continuation.path.json","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T18:21:05.934884Z","id":"7c886f861585160c859e45f182899a9cc41bb6cb60ba4351d9b4edd46bf5e471","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:271b751","summary":"examples/path-05-continuation.path.json step-004 hunk is '@@ -27,0 +28,3 @@' with three added lines (a one-line Default impl); step-007 is '@@ -28,3 +28,5 @@' and expands it the way rustfmt would, so Auto-format changes something (p render md reports src/lib.rs (+3 -1)). Same raw in examples/path-05-continuation.path.jsonl. p validate passes.","supersedes":"64f730cf5b3f2df5813382c12fe88af7b11f2934020e9ddc6f3743aa50e38cb1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"examples/path-05-continuation.path.json","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:10:59.563670Z","id":"043cf02d3ec1df735038b2ae89034a444705d32d5ad941e66399ecc147390adc","body":{"detail":"RFC.md (Base Context, around line 633) now defines path.base as 'the state of the artifacts the work started from'. In examples/path-05-continuation.path.json (and the matching PathOpen line in .path.jsonl) base is {uri: file:///home/alex/projects/myrepo, ref: def789abc123456}, the same base as examples/path-02-local-session.path.json. But path-02's steps step-001..step-003 add struct Config and impl Config::from_env to src/lib.rs, and path-05's first step (step-004) applies '@@ -27,0 +28,3 @@' to src/lib.rs, a hunk that only lines up after those edits. So the state path-05 started from is def789 plus path-02's work, not def789. The example is the project's demonstration of how parent and base sit together, and it shows them disagreeing. Readers copying it will record the original commit as base for every resumed session, so a tool that checks out base and replays the diffs gets hunks that do not apply.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":9},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"e10fe0078239d00d2b93fc11f3ce320837d548f71dd0f29676959453ed8dc450"},"suggested_fix":"Make the example consistent with the base definition: either drop base from path-05 (the starting state is fully determined by parent plus path-02's own base), or give it a base that really is the starting state, and add one sentence to RFC.md Path Parent saying which a continuation writer should do when the parent's work was never committed.","summary":"The continuation example's base names commit def789abc123456, but its work starts from that commit plus path-session-xyz's uncommitted edits, which is not what the RFC now says base means","tags":["review","review:pr-354-qual-2","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"examples/path-05-continuation.path.json","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:14:02.168941Z","id":"e67dd4b3ce9a987b2d6382b7b924889f5d625b65fa83b80a113a23ddff9e68a0","body":{"detail":"examples/path-05-continuation.path.json:9-12 has base {uri: file:///home/alex/projects/myrepo, ref: def789abc123456}. examples/path-02-local-session.path.json:9-11 has the same base, and path-02 has three steps that change src/lib.rs: step-001 '@@ -1,3 +1,10 @@' adds struct Config, step-002 '@@ -8,0 +9,15 @@' adds impl Config::from_env, step-003 '@@ -12,4 +12,5 @@'. path-05 step-004 applies '@@ -27,0 +28,3 @@ +impl Default for Config { fn default() -> Self { Self::from_env() } }' to src/lib.rs. That hunk needs line 27 and Config::from_env to exist, so it only applies after path-02's edits. The PathOpen line in examples/path-05-continuation.path.jsonl:1 carries the same base. RFC.md:633-634 says path.base 'records the state of the artifacts the work started from', and the owner decision on d75fa1ac (reply 221e2fe7) says the same. So the example's base contradicts the definition. Concern is the right kind: this is the reference example people will copy, but no code fails on it.","kind":"comment","references":"043cf02d3ec1df735038b2ae89034a444705d32d5ad941e66399ecc147390adc","summary":"confirmed: path-05's base is def789abc123456, the same base path-02 starts from, but its first hunk only applies after path-02's edits","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"examples/path-05-continuation.path.json","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T18:55:20.722358Z","id":"151ed5cb20d5467b85731a9047bb60dadc3ff625f0b085081a2574979d8f7369","body":{"detail":"Owner decision, 2026-10-13: 'base is for project context like it was originally designed for. we have parent for continuations now.' main's RFC defined base as 'the root context (repo, commit) a path branches from'; this PR reworded it to 'the artifact state the work started from' (RFC.md:72, 625, 633-634, 204), which is what made the example look wrong. Under the original meaning a continuation legitimately shares its parent's base commit: both sessions ran against the same project state, and parent, not base, says whose edits come first. examples/path-05 stays as written. The toolpath: base form stays as an alternative uri for a project whose state is tracked in Toolpath rather than a VCS (owner decision of 2026-10-07), described as project context, not as lineage.","kind":"decision","references":"043cf02d3ec1df735038b2ae89034a444705d32d5ad941e66399ecc147390adc","suggested_fix":"In RFC.md restore the base wording to project context: the glossary row (:72), the field list (:625), the Base Context intro (:633-634) and the parent/base contrast sentence (:204; 'parent is lineage; base is the project context the path ran against'). Keep the Toolpath Base subsection but phrase it as project context in Toolpath. Leave examples/path-05 unchanged; optionally add one sentence under Path Parent noting a continuation usually shares its parent's base. Rides along in the #354 fix pass.","summary":"Decided: the example is right; the RFC's redefinition of base is what changes back. base is project context (the repo state a path branches from), parent is lineage","tags":["review:pr-354-qual-2","decision","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
